wayland-server: build with wayland-protocols' text-input-v3 version 2

text-input-unstable-v3 version 2 (wayland-protocols 1.49, the version
HaikuPorts has) adds three requests, set_available_actions,
show_input_panel and hide_input_panel, which the generated C++ interface
declares pure virtual: HaikuTextInput was abstract and did not compile.
They are implemented as no-ops. The global still offers version 1, so
clients do not send them.

--- a/HaikuTextInput.h	2025-10-04 05:05:06.000000000 +0200
+++ b/HaikuTextInput.h	2026-10-21 11:12:49.822952442 +0200
@@ -32,6 +32,9 @@
 	void HandleSetContentType(uint32_t hint, uint32_t purpose) final;
 	void HandleSetCursorRectangle(int32_t x, int32_t y, int32_t width, int32_t height) final;
 	void HandleCommit() final;
+	void HandleSetAvailableActions(struct wl_array *availableActions) final;
+	void HandleShowInputPanel() final;
+	void HandleHideInputPanel() final;
 };
 
 
--- a/HaikuTextInput.cpp	2025-10-04 05:05:06.000000000 +0200
+++ b/HaikuTextInput.cpp	2026-10-21 11:13:03.164222387 +0200
@@ -251,3 +251,18 @@
 
 	fGlobal->SendState(this);
 }
+
+// text-input-v3 version 2 requests: the global offers version 1, so clients do not send them, and
+// Haiku has no on-screen input panel to show or hide
+
+void HaikuTextInput::HandleSetAvailableActions(struct wl_array *availableActions)
+{
+}
+
+void HaikuTextInput::HandleShowInputPanel()
+{
+}
+
+void HaikuTextInput::HandleHideInputPanel()
+{
+}
